ier Prime',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Courier Prime</span><small>Typed-page feel</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="plexmono"><b style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Plex Mono</span><small>Even, technical</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="specialelite"><b style="font-family:'Special Elite',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Special Elite</span><small>Worn typewriter</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="cutive"><b style="font-family:'Cutive Mono',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Cutive Mono</span><small>Light, old typewriter</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="spacemono"><b style="font-family:'Space Mono',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Space Mono</span><small>Quirky retro mono</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="jetbrains"><b style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>JetBrains Mono</span><small>Roomy, clear mono</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="robotomono"><b style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Roboto Mono</span><small>Neat and even</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="inconsolata"><b style="font-family:'Inconsolata',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Inconsolata</span><small>Slim, classic mono</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="sourcecode"><b style="font-family:'Source Code Pro',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Source Code</span><small>Clean code mono</small></button><button type="button" data-fn="overpass"><b style="font-family:'Overpass Mono',var(--serif)">Aa</b><span>Overpass Mono</span><small>Soft highway mono</small></button></div></details></template><!-- polish-2026-10: the other faces live in the template above; restore one by moving its button into the grid and adding its key to POLISH_FONT_KEEP --></div><select id="fnt" hidden aria-label="Font"><option value="theme">Match theme</option><option value="serif">Newsreader</option><option value="literata">Literata</option><option value="garamond">Garamond</option><option value="source">Source Serif 4</option><option value="lora">Lora</option><option value="sans">Instrument</option><option value="inter">Inter</option><option value="lexend">Lexend</option><option value="hyper">Atkinson</option><option value="dys">OpenDyslexic</option><option value="courierprime">Courier Prime</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Type preset<small>One tap sets font, spacing and alignment together</small></span><div class="segs tp" id="tpre"><button data-tp="editorial">Editorial</button><button data-tp="modern">Modern</button><button data-tp="classic">Classic</button><button data-tp="calm">Calm</button></div></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Headline font<small>Titles and headlines across the app</small></span><select id="hfn"><option value="serif">Match theme</option><option value="playfair">Playfair Display</option><option value="garamond">Garamond</option><option value="cormorant">Cormorant</option><option value="fraunces">Fraunces</option><option value="sans">Sans</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Reading style<small>Turn pages like a magazine, or scroll down. Automatic scrolls on narrow screens and when a story opens beside the list</small></span><div class="segs" id="scs"><button data-sc="auto">Automatic</button><button data-sc="pages">Pages</button><button data-sc="vertical">Scroll</button></div></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Text size<small>Use the buttons to make reading text bigger or smaller</small></span><span class="ctl"><button class="ib" data-fs="-1" aria-label="Smaller"><span style="font-size:12px">A</span></button><b id="fsv"></b><button class="ib" data-fs="1" aria-label="Larger"><span style="font-size:18px">A</span></button></span></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Line spacing<small>The space between lines of text</small></span><select id="lhs"><option value="1.5">Tight</option><option value="1.68">Normal</option><option value="1.9">Roomy</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Page margins<small>The empty space at the sides of the page</small></span><select id="mgn"><option value="0.6">Narrow</option><option value="1">Normal</option><option value="1.6">Wide</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Compact reading on phones<small>Uses more of the screen: narrower margins, tighter lines, even left edge and a smaller first letter. Off keeps your own margin, spacing and justify settings</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="pcomp"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Justify text<small>Even edges, like a printed page</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="just"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Bold word starts<small>Bolds the first letters of every word so your eye can skim along the line. Helps some people with focus or dyslexia</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="focusr"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Dim photos in dark themes<small>Softens bright pictures in stories when the page is dark, so they don’t glare</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="pdim"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Author and site notes<small>Bios and site blurbs at the start or end of a story. Fold tucks them into a small note you can open, Hide removes them, Leave as is shows them in the story</small></span><select id="bfs"><option value="fold">Fold away</option><option value="hide">Hide completely</option><option value="off">Leave as is</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Magazine touches<small>Drop caps and pull quotes in longer stories</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="mag"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Follow my phone’s text size<small>The reader scales with the text size set in your phone’s settings</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="sysfs"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Continuous reading<small>Keep pulling past the end of a story (or turn the last page again) to flow straight into the next one</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="cont"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Keep back issues<small>Off by default. Keeps each edition’s text, only from stories already stored on this device, so you can browse old issues like a magazine rack. Nothing extra is downloaded</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="bi"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Keep back issues for<small>Older issues are removed automatically</small></span><select id="bid"><option value="30">30 days</option><option value="90">90 days</option><option value="180">180 days</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Polished typography<small>Curly quotes and proper dashes in stories</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="typo"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Sepia reading page<small>Warm paper in the reader only</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="sep"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Tint pages with photo colors<small>Covers and story pages pick up the main color of the photo</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="ptint"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Page-turn sound<small>A soft paper rustle</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="tsound"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Page-turn tick<small>A tiny vibration when a page lands</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="thaptic"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Swipe down to close a story<small>Pull a story down to go back to the list</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="sdown"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Swipe a card to the left<small>What a swipe toward the left does to a story card</small></span><select id="swlsel" aria-label="Swipe a card to the left"><option value="save">Save or unsave</option><option value="read">Mark read or unread</option><option value="off">Nothing</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Swipe a card to the right<small>What a swipe toward the right does to a story card</small></span><select id="swrsel" aria-label="Swipe a card to the right"><option value="save">Save or unsave</option><option value="read">Mark read or unread</option><option value="off">Nothing</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Read as you scroll<small>A story counts as read once its card has scrolled up off the screen. Off unless you turn it on</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="rdscroll"></button></div><div class="line" id="aist" hidden><span class="lb">AI summary<small id="aisx"></small></span></div></div></section>
  <section class="sgrp" id="s-mag"><h3><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="17" height="17" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 4h11l3 3v13H5z"/><path d="M8 9h8M8 13h8M8 17h5"/></svg>Magazine and digest</h3><div class="sbox"><div class="line"><span class="lb">Table of contents<small>An “In this issue” list on The Daily, with page numbers you can tap</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="toc"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Feature spread<small>One big story per issue with an oversized headline</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="spread"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Story layout on big screens<small>How the first pages of a story are laid out when the screen is wide. Automatic picks per story</small></span><select id="rlay"><option value="auto">Automatic</option><option value="hero">Hero spread</option><option value="top">Photo on top</option><option value="split">Photo and text</option><option value="classic">Classic columns</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Section covers<small>A folder, site or topic opens with a title, photo and a line about what’s inside</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="sop"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Story timeline<small>When several sites cover the same story, see who reported it first and how it developed</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="tline"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Cinematic long reads<small>Long stories scrolled down the page open with a full-width photo; pictures drift gently against the text and sections get big headings. Turn off if scrolling feels heavy</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="cine"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Tidy photo captions<small>Captions in small type, with the photo credit set apart underneath</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="caps"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">At-a-glance box<small>On a hero or split opening, a small box with the source, date, reading time and who else covered it</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="mnote"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">You might also like<small>At the end of a story, a few links from sites you don’t follow yet that match its subject, with a Follow button</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="disc"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Varied story layout<small>A mix of big photos, headline lists, strips and quotes that changes by feed and day, instead of equal squares. Choose Compact or Narrow cards to keep the classic grid</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="nroom"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Trending strip<small>A row of stories that several sources covered at once, at the top of The Daily</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="trend"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Must reads<small>On wide screens, a ranked list of your top stories next to the front page</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="must"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Edition endings<small>A brass seal and a closing line at the end of each edition, brief and long-reads list</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="seal"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Bookmark ribbons<small>A brass ribbon on stories you saved, and a thin line showing how far you read</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="rib"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">I have 10 minutes<small>A button on The Daily that builds a short issue to fit the time you have</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="ten"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Monthly tidy-up note<small>Once a month at most, a note about sites that went quiet or never load</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="tidy"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Year almanac<small>A card on The Daily from December 1 to January 15 with your year in reading</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="alm"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Seasonal touches<small>A small detail on the cypress mark that changes with the seasons</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="szn"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Story pull quotes<small>A line pulled from a story, set big between sections</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="pqc"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Light rays on the cover<small>A soft glow in the cover photo’s color behind the masthead</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="cray"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Cover title style<small>Auto looks at each cover photo and picks the style that reads best on it. Or choose one for every cover: Clean is plain white, Tinted and Gradient pick up color, Glow lights it up</small></span><select id="mast"><option value="auto">Auto (best for each photo)</option><option value="clean">Clean</option><option value="tint">Tinted</option><option value="glow">Glow</option><option value="gradient">Gradient</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Quiet layout<small>More white space, muted photos and no badges, for a calmer front page</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="quiet"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Photo pages<small>Stories with many big photos give some of them a whole page</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="fbleed"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Pull quotes on The Daily<small>A quote from your own highlights between sections</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="pqs"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Page numbers in stories<small>A small running line with the site, title and page at the foot of each page</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="folio"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">End-of-story mark<small>A small mark at the end of each story</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="endm"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Daily digest<small>A daily issue with a cover story, your topics, saved stories and what you missed. Works offline</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="dgon"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Digest edition<small>Offer the morning issue, the evening issue, or both on The Daily</small></span><select id="dgwhen"><option value="morning">Morning</option><option value="evening">Evening</option><option value="both">Morning and evening</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Weekly review<small>A longer issue with your reading stats</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="dgwk"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Weekly review day<small>The day the weekly issue comes out</small></span><select id="dgwd"><option value="0">Sunday</option><option value="1">Monday</option><option value="6">Saturday</option><option value="5">Friday</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Read today’s digest<small>Opens today’s digest right now</small></span><button class="tx2" id="dgopen">Open</button></div></div></section>
  <section class="sgrp" id="s-tts"><h3><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="17" height="17" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10v4h3.5L12 18V6L7.5 10z"/><path d="M15.5 9a4 4 0 0 1 0 6M18 6.5a8 8 0 0 1 0 11"/></svg>Read aloud</h3><div class="sbox"><div class="line"><span class="lb">Voice help<small>What to say to Google, and routines</small></span><button class="tx2" id="vhopen">Show</button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Voice<small>The voice that reads stories aloud</small></span><select id="voice"></select></div><p class="hint" id="novoice" hidden style="padding:0 16px 10px"></p><div class="line" id="nvw" hidden><span class="lb">Natural voice<small id="nvh"></small></span><span class="ctl"><select id="nvz" aria-label="Natural voice size"><option value="phone">Off</option><option value="compact">Compact</option><option value="full">Full</option></select><button type="button" class="tx2" id="nvdel" aria-label="Delete the natural voice" hidden>Delete</button></span></div><div class="line" id="sayln" hidden><span class="lb">Fix how words are said<small id="sayn">Teach the voice names and words it gets wrong</small></span><button type="button" class="tx2" id="sayb">Fix words</button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Second voice for quotes<small>Reads quoted speech in a different voice</small></span><select id="qv"></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Speaking speed<small>How fast stories are read aloud</small></span><span class="rng"><input type="range" id="rate" min="0.6" max="2" step="0.1"><output id="ratev"></output></span></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Volume<small>How loud stories are read aloud</small></span><span class="rng"><input type="range" id="vol" min="0" max="1" step="0.05"><output id="volv"></output></span></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Keep playing<small>When one story finishes, read the next one in the list</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="queue"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Read photo captions<small>Off: the voice skips the small text under pictures</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="ttscap"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Skip subscriber sites<small>Play the Daily leaves out sites that need a subscription, so everything you hear is the full story</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="skippay"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Voice timing<small>If the highlighted word seems to run ahead of or behind the voice, this clears what CyPress learned about your voice and lets it work it out again</small></span><button type="button" class="tx2" id="vtreset">Reset</button></div></div></section>
- <section class="sgrp" id="s-stories"><h3><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="17" height="17" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="13" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="4" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="13" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/></svg>Stories</h3><div class="sbox"><div class="line"><span class="lb">Limit per site<small>The most stories one site can show on The Daily and All Stories, so a busy site can’t crowd out the rest</small></span><select id="capn"><option value="0">No limit</option><option value="3">3</option><option value="5">5</option><option value="8">8</option><option value="12">12</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Order of feeds and folders<small>As you added them, or A to Z in the sidebar and lists</small></span><select id="fsrt"><option value="">As added</option><option value="az">A to Z</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Order of stories<small>Best stories first, newest first, or grouped by the site they come from</small></span><select id="srt"><option value="smart">Best first</option><option value="new">Newest first</option><option value="source">By site</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Shorten shared links<small>When you share a story, its link is made short by CyPress's own link service. If it is off, or the service does not answer, the story's own web address is shared</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="shortlinks"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Group duplicate stories<small>One card when several sites cover it</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="group"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Hide stories I’ve read<small>Stories you’ve opened disappear from the list</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="hideRead"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Quiet mode: dots, not numbers<small>Shows a small dot beside feeds and folders with something new, in place of the unread counts. Also hides “unread” in The Daily</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="hideCount"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Muted words<small>Hide stories that mention them</small></span><button class="tx2" id="mut">Edit</button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Followed phrases<small id="fwl">Stories that mention them move up and are marked. With story alerts on, new ones send a notification</small></span><button class="tx2" id="fwe" aria-label="Edit followed phrases">Edit</button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Hide deals and shopping<small>Hide stories that are really ads, like “30% off” or “best deals” roundups. It’s a best guess, so a real story can occasionally slip through</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="hideDeals"></button></div><div class="line" id="dealsrow" hidden><span class="lb">What’s hidden<small id="dealsn"></small></span><button class="tx2" id="dealsee">See</button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">What CyPress learned<small>The sites and headline words your “More like this” and “Less like this” taps have taught it. Forget any of them</small></span><button class="tx2" id="lrnsee">See</button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Check sites before adding<small>Looks at a few stories first and warns you if a site mostly posts links, hasn’t posted lately, or may not open properly. You can still add it</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="fcheck"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Topics you follow<small>Collect stories by keyword, from every site</small></span><button class="tx2" id="sfb">Manage</button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Double-tap a card to save it<small>Opening a story waits a moment so the app can tell the difference</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="dtap"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Single-key shortcuts<small>J, K, S, N, P, F and the others. Turn off if a key press is easy to hit by mistake, for example with voice control</small></span><button class="tg" data-tg="keysOn"></button></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Kindle books<small>Black and white suits e-ink Kindles. Color suits the Kindle Colorsoft, Kobo Clara Color and phones</small></span><select id="kmode" aria-label="Kindle book style"><option value="bw">Black and white</option><option value="color">Color</option></select></div><div class="line"><span class="lb">Your Kindle address<small id="kaddr">Not set yet</small></span><button class="tx2" id="kset">Change</button></div></div></section>
